", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 66 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Open seat: John James (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 10th District is an open seat after Republican John James left to run for governor, and both parties treat it as a pivot point for House control. The district leans Republican on paper, but the national political environment favors Democrats this year. Democrat Christina Hines has out-raised Republican Mike Bouchard Jr. and benefits from outside spending, including a $1 million Giffords PAC investment, while Bouchard, a Bronze Star veteran, entered with a strong biography and roughly comparable cash on hand.\n\nMost expert ratings call the race a Democratic lean or a tossup, and prediction markets price Hines around a two-in-three favorite. Available polling is sparse, dated, and sponsored by Democratic groups, and it shows the candidates tied. The forecast gives Hines a modest edge, with wide uncertainty typical of a low-data open seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6628, "margin": 2.54}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6491, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6831, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6477, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.623, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5903, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6399, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6806, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6694, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7119, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6799, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6842, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6979, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6212, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6272, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6412, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6477, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_